id: pm-gh1573
title: "GH-1573: await telemetry producers before Sentry fixture cleanup"
description: "Ubuntu Node22 nightly run40079265521 failed the intentional scope and parameter privacy tracing case during owned-root deletion (ENOTEMPTY under global/locks). The fixture deliberately clears test signals and therefore permits normal detached telemetry delivery. Establish producer lifetime and await delivery before cleanup while retaining consent/privacy/native-test controls. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1573"
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: github,nightly-regression,telemetry,testing
created_at: "2026-10-24T09:44:39.464Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T10:10:03.038Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#67ddd7c5bf7e85e8f28aa1ff"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Retain intentional loopback tracing and all privacy and consent assertions; Bind fixture delivery to foreground completion before deleting owned roots; Pass the affected telemetry suite and hosted Ubuntu Node22 shard without deleting or suppressing existing regression coverage
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: 75
expected_result: "Fixture command completion also settles its telemetry producer, preserving real delivery and deterministic cleanup."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T09:44:39.464Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full strict corpus3094 items has no implementation owner for GH1573. Live open/in_progress and Sentry tracing cleanup search read; pm-2zjs0g is the closed measurement owner and pm-gh1484 is the completed native-test inference repair. Neither owns this intentional-delivery fixture lifetime. Retain original failure as historical evidence."
  "2026-10-24T09:48:24.638Z","harness:codex","Confirmed lifetime mechanism: clearing VITEST/NODE_ENV in the intentional tracing child selects the ordinary scheduleTelemetryFlush detached-spawn branch. The existing custom-harness opt-in PM_TELEMETRY_INLINE_FLUSH=1 selects serialized awaited delivery before finishTelemetryCommand returns. The fixture now uses that contract, routes loopback event batches separately from Sentry envelopes, asserts ordered command_start/command_finish and an empty physical event queue, and retains all consent/privacy/native-test controls. Focused 18-case telemetry suite passes; no production inference or cleanup retry was introduced."
  "2026-10-24T09:50:04.279Z","harness:codex","Independent negative control in a detached temporary checkout: the unchanged strengthened scope/privacy test with PM_TELEMETRY_INLINE_FLUSH=0 fails because no command_start/command_finish reaches the collector before child completion (expected pair, observed empty array). Setting only the explicit inline-delivery option to1 passes the same assertions in the main checkout. This demonstrates lifetime sensitivity without changing consent/privacy checks, sleeping, polling, or retrying recursive deletion."
